We can profile this converted model by creating an inference session with profiling
enabled, as explained in section 9.1:
from onnxruntime import InferenceSession, SessionOptions
so = SessionOptions()
so.enable_profiling = True
sess = InferenceSession(model_def.SerializeToString(), so)
We’ll run inference over the test set (111 samples) and stop profiling at the end:
sess.run(None, {'X': X_test})
prof = sess.end_profiling()
The raw profiling data can now be loaded from the JSON file:
import json
with open(prof, "r") as f:
    js = json.load(f)
Next, we’ll create a pandas DataFrame from them:
from mlprodict.onnxrt.ops_whole.session import OnnxWholeSession
df = pd.DataFrame(OnnxWholeSession.process_profiling(js))

