Chapter 11  Deployment and serving
llm = LLM(model=model_id, device=device, dtype=torch.half)
sampling_params = SamplingParams(temperature=0.5)
The only thing that changes is the method we call. Given a conversation prompt like
the following
conversation = [
    {
        "role": "system",
        "content": "You are a helpful assistant"
    },
    {
        "role": "user",
        "content": "Hi"
    },
    {
        "role": "assistant",
        "content": "Hi! How can I assist you today?"
    },
    {
        "role": "user",
        "content": "Write an essay about the Monte Carlo Tree Search
        ➥ algorithm.",
    },
]
the method we’ll use is chat:
outputs = llm.chat(conversation,
                   sampling_params=sampling_params,
                   use_tqdm=False)
The chat method works for both single and batch inference:
conversations = [conversation for _ in range(10)]
outputs = llm.chat(messages=conversations,
                   sampling_params=sampling_params,
                   use_tqdm=True)
We can also provide an optional chat template. For example, to use the following Jinja
template with the Phi-3 Mini 4K Instruct model, save it as phi-3.jinja:
{% if messages[0]['role'] == 'system' %}
    {% set offset = 1 %}
{% else %}
    {% set offset = 0 %}
{% endif %}
{% for message in messages %}
